WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Here is a coil of shiny
wire with no label.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.410
Is it copper, iron, or some special alloy?

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.330
You have no chemicals and no lab tests.

4
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.120
Just a long ruler, a micrometer,
an ammeter and a voltmeter.

5
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:20.110
Every wire has a resistance, but a long
thin wire has more than a short thick

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:20.810
one.

7
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.930
So resistance alone cannot name the metal.

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.070
So what can these tools measure
that belongs to the metal itself?

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.440
In this mission, you'll measure the
diameter at several points and use a sliding

10
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.320
clip to set the length.

11
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.730
Then you'll see why a graph
beats a single reading.

12
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: work out how simple
measurements reveal what a wire is made of.
